{"parentUuid":"e8fada06-50ad-4d34-ad5f-12023e641851","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DL3NhNDxkco1YbeYQRsPBY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking at `cmd/entire/cli/api/client.go:70-91`, `GetStream` does duplicate the flow in `c.do` — URL resolve → `NewRequestWithContext` → `c.httpClient.Do` — with two real differences:\n\n1. It threads through caller-supplied `headers` (needed for `Accept: text/event-stream` and `Last-Event-ID`).\n2. It deliberately skips the `Content-Type: application/json` that `c.do` sets — but `c.do` only sets it when `body != nil`, and `GetStream` always passes `nil`, so this would be a no-op either way.\n\nSo yes, it could share `c.do`. The cleanest refactor is to extend `c.do` to accept an optional `http.Header` and have `GetStream` delegate:\n\n```go\nfunc (c *Client) do(ctx context.Context, method, path string, body io.Reader, headers http.Header) (*http.Response, error) {\n    // ... existing URL/request build ...\n    for k, vs := range headers {\n        for _, v := range vs { req.Header.Add(k, v) }\n    }\n    if body != nil { req.Header.Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\") }\n    // ... existing dispatch ...\n}\n\nfunc (c *Client) GetStream(ctx context.Context, path string, headers http.Header) (*http.Response, error) {\n    return c.do(ctx, http.MethodGet, path, nil, headers)\n}\n```\n\nTrade-off: every existing caller (`Get`/`Post`/`Put`/`Patch`/`Delete`) gains a `nil` arg, but you get one code path for URL resolution + request creation + error wrapping. Given there are five existing callers and the duplication is only ~10 lines, it's a judgment call — I'd lean toward doing it because right now any change to `c.do` (e.g., adding a request hook, tracing, retry logic) silently skips streaming requests.\n\nWorth noting the error wrap is inconsistent too: `c.do` returns `\"%s %s: %w\"` (method+path); `GetStream` hardcodes `\"GET %s: %w\"`. Unifying them