Do Pattern\n\nThe go-github library provides `NewRequest` and `NewUploadRequest` methods on the Client. \n\nPackage github provides a client for using the GitHub API. To use it, you construct a new GitHub client, then use the various services on the client to access different parts of the GitHub API.\n\nThe typical pattern involves:\n\n1. **Creating a request**: The `client.NewRequest(method, urlStr string, body interface{})` method returns an `*http.Request`\n\n2. **Executing the request**: The client has a `bareDo` method for executing requests\n\nThe underlying architecture follows a common Go HTTP client pattern where custom headers are created using NewRequest and Client.Do.\n\nFor practical usage, you construct a new GitHub client and then use various services on the client to access different parts of the GitHub API, for example: `client := github.NewClient(nil)` followed by service method calls like `client.Organizations.List(ctx, \"willnorris\", nil)`.\n\nThis pattern separates request construction from execution, allowing for flexibility in adding headers, modifying the request before sending, and handling responses consistently across the library.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4f1c661c-112a-4266-8c30-bf5380c5b782","timestamp":"2026-05-11T10:34:44.945Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"\"go-github\" client.NewRequest client.Do source code pattern","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UqwtMje5yeXs6w1eamkcmV","content":[{"title":"GitHub - google/go-github: Go library for accessing the GitHub v3 API · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/google/go-github"},{"title":"go/src/net/http/client.go at master · golang/go","url":"https://github.com/golang/go/blob/master/src/net/http/client.go"},{"title":"github package - github.com/google/go-github/github - Go Packages","url":"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/google/go-github/github"},{"title":"go/src/net/http/request.go at master · golang/go"