{"parentUuid":"7c8997c4-79aa-4dbf-b0f5-2c897765c344","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01B5fBoz8xA4e5VePvyAkJBz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick findings:\n\n**In this codebase:** no precedent — `GetStream` is the only method like this.\n\n**In the Go ecosystem**, three patterns dominate, and `GetWithHeaders` isn't really one of them:\n\n1. **Construct-then-execute** (go-github, kubernetes/client-go, AWS SDK, most \"professional\" clients): the public surface is `NewRequest(ctx, method, path, body) (*http.Request, error)` + `Do(req, v) (*http.Response, error)`. Headers go on the request, not the method name. `Get`/`Post` are thin convenience wrappers over `NewRequest`+`Do`.\n\n2. **Fluent/builder** (resty, sling): `client.R().SetHeader(\"X\",\"Y\").Get(path)`. No `WithHeaders` suffix — headers are chained off a request builder.\n\n3. **Functional options**: `client.Get(ctx, path, WithHeader(\"X\",\"Y\"))`. Less common.\n\nThe `WithHeader[s]` *method name* shows up mostly in builder-style libraries (e.g. ddliu/go-httpclient) as chainable setters returning the receiver — not as `GetWithHeaders` returning a response.\n\n**So pragmatically for our case:**\n\n- **If you expect this to be a one-off** (SSE is the only special caller): `GetWithHeaders` is fine. It's not idiomatic-with-a-capital-I, but it's instantly readable and the cost of refactoring later if we get more callers is tiny.\n- **If you expect 2-3 more headers-needing callers** (conditional GETs, idempotency keys, etc.): switch to the go-github shape — expose `NewRequest`+`Do` and reduce `Get`/`Post`/etc. to convenience wrappers. That's the pattern that ages best in Go.\n\nFor an internal client at this scale (5 methods, ~150 lines, one consumer needing headers), I'd just do `GetWithHeaders` and revisit if a third caller appears. Don't over-engineer it.\n\nSources:\n- [google/go-github source](https://github.com/google/go-github/blob/master/github/github.go) — `NewRequest`+`Do` pattern\n- [ddliu/go-httpclient](https://github.com/ddliu/go-httpclient) — `WithHeader`/`WithHeaders` as builder setters\n- [Configuring the Go HTTP client — LogRocket](https://blog.logrocket.com/configuring-the-go-http-client/)\n- [Build an HTTP Client — Practical Go Lessons](https://www.practical-go-lessons.com/chap-35-build-an-http-client)\n- [net/http package — Go Packages](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":82026,"output_tokens":1693,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1693,"cache_read_input_tokens":82026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CavdcbWYMPE9VAzFmT591","type":"assistant","uuid":"036f75b3-4f6f-4c76-83b4-f9240aa21d23","timestamp":"2026-05-11T10:35:05.646Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"4d570a00-2bde-45d9-a871-46c43fdae1d4","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"feat/trail-watch-sse"}
